package kgen

// opsZones is the core OPS.md family for zone changes, library placement, tokens and copies. opsEntries (opsdoc.go)
// places it in the document; a new item goes in its own opsdoc_<mechanic>.go.
var opsZones = []opsDoc{
	{"op:ExileEx", "OpExileEx (Obj, A counters, B.N counter kind, C MoveFlags)", "Exile Obj (from whatever zone it is in). MvRemember: the exiled objects become the remembered set (RefRemembered). A>0: the card is exiled with A counters of kind B.N (Tinybones' stash counter). MvForgetChanged: the exiled object leaves the remembered set again (ForgetChanged$ True)."},
	{"op:ReturnEx", "OpReturnEx (Obj, A counters, B.N kind, C zone|MoveFlags<<3)", "Move Obj from graveyard/exile to zone `C&7`, under its owner's control unless MvUnderYourControl (then the resolving controller's). MvTapped: enters tapped. A>0: enters with A counters of kind B.N (an as-enters modification, not an event after entering — Infernal Vessel, Valkyrie's Call, Nine-Lives Familiar). A constant A may add a second kind: A = count | (second kind + 1)<<8 (kop.RetCounterPairShift), and the permanent enters with count counters of B.N then of the second kind (WithCountersType$ with two kinds — Perennation). A following OpOverride with Obj = the same ref applies to the object it became. MvForgetChanged (ForgetChanged$ True, gorge eventForgetChanged): the returned object leaves the resolution's remembered set, order kept (after MvRemember, which would re-add it). MvEntryRiders' bit (C's sign bit; Origin$ All on a Defined$ Remembered move): a library card moves too, which every other OpReturnEx skips (Turntimber Symbiosis's counter-bearing put of the card its dig set on top of the library). B.N RetFromLibrary (Origin$ Library, a Defined$ library fetch): only a library card moves; B.N RetShuffleOwed (the script owes a shuffle: a preceding Shuffle$ False search deferred it, or Shuffle$ True) shuffles its owner's library after the move (gorge moveDefinedLibraryObjects: a Defined$ fetch is not a search); Guidelight Pathmaker, Archdruid's Charm. B.N RetUnderOpponent (GainControl$ ChosenPlayer after a one-opponent ChoosePlayer, CR 110.2a; never with A counters): the object enters under the resolving controller's opponent; Zuko, Conflicted. B.N RetAttachTo (AttachedTo$; never with A counters): B bits 8..10 name the bearer Ref (Self, or the target slot of ParentTarget). The returned Aura enters attached to it when it is among the Aura's legal objects to enchant, else stays in its zone (CR 303.4g); an Equipment enters, then attaches when the bearer is a creature on the battlefield; Eagle's Rescue, Magnetic Snuffler."},
	{"c:LibTopShuffle", "OpToLibrary C = kop.LibTopShuffle", "The object goes on top of its owner's library, then that library is shuffled, even when the object did not move while it exists (gorge effChangeZone's object path with Shuffle$ True, objectPathShuffleOwners; CR 701.24c). Alabaster Dragon."},
	{"c:LibThird", "OpToLibrary C = kop.LibThird", "The object goes into its owner's library third from the top (LibraryPosition$ 2): min(2, the other cards left) cards sit above it (gorge libraryOrderPlacementAt). Braided Quipu."},
	{"c:LibTopShuffleGrave", "OpToLibrary C = kop.LibTopShuffleGrave", "LibTopShuffle for a trigger object's Origin$ Graveyard move: the card moves and the library is shuffled only if the card is still in the graveyard; exiled in response, neither happens (gorge's Origin$ precondition on the object path). Lembas."},
	{"c:LibBottomShuffle", "OpToLibrary C = kop.LibBottomShuffle", "LibTopShuffle with LibraryPosition$ -1: the object goes on the bottom of its owner's library, then that library is shuffled (gorge effChangeZone's object path). Unlucky Cabbage Merchant."},
	{"op:ToLibraryChoice", "OpToLibraryChoice (Obj)", "Decision for Obj's OWNER: top (C = kop.LibChoiceSecond: second from the top, min(1, the other cards) above it) or bottom of their library; then move it there. Uncharted Voyage (AlternativeDecider$ TargetedOwner); Temporal Cleansing (LibraryPosition$ 1)."},
	{"op:SearchEx", "OpSearchEx (Obj player, A count, C zone|SearchFlags<<3, F)", "Player searches their library for up to A cards matching F (zone Library) and puts them in zone `C&7` (Hand, Battlefield, or Library for SrThenTop), then shuffles. SrTapped: they enter tapped. SrThenTop: shuffle, then put the found card on top (Campus Guide). SrMandatory: must find one if able (gorge Mandatory$: Grim Tutor, Rune-Scarred Demon). SrRemember: the found cards join the remembered set (RememberChanged$, gorge zone_search eventRemember: Fabled Passage's untap); kgen refuses it with a library destination or SrThenTop. The shuffle is mandatory, even when nothing was found (CR 701.23, 701.24c/d; gorge): ShuffleNonMandatory$ lowers to nothing and SrShuffleOptional is retired. SrForgetChanged (B bit 1; ForgetChanged$ True): each found card that moved leaves the remembered set again (Troop of Ponies' pick). SrNoShuffle (B; Shuffle$ False): no shuffle after the moves, a library destination putting the found cards on top with the first answered on top, remembered with SrRemember (Cultivate, Flourishing Bloom-Kin). SrAltOrigin (B bit 4; OriginAlternative$): B bits 5..7 name the alternative zone (Graveyard or Hand), or SrAltGraveHand for the Graveyard,Hand pair; the searcher first elects the zones to search (ChGenKczZone: the library and the alternatives, closed by Done), the pool is the elected zones' matching cards library first, and the library is shuffled only when it was elected (Delivery Moogle, Last Light of Durin's Day; Agency Outfitter's pair with SrDifferentNames). SrAltAll (B bit 3, with SrAltOrigin and the Graveyard zone; Origin$ Library,Graveyard): the election is settled as both zones, nobody is asked, and the library is shuffled (Journey for the Elixir, Verdant Crescendo). SrSideboard (B bit 10; ChangeZone Origin$ Sideboard / Library,Sideboard, CR 400.11): the pool also holds the searcher's sideboard cards (the cards outside the game they own, object order) after the library; SrNoLibrary (B bit 11) leaves the library out (no look, no shuffle, ChGenSearch); DifferentNames$ counts the names over the whole pool. SrExactly (B bit 2; Exactly$ True): exactly A cards are found or none (Done is offered only before the first pick). SrChooserOpp (B bit 0; Chooser$ Opponent): the opponent answers the picks. A zone-none destination finds and, with SrRemember, remembers the cards where they lie (Turtles Forever's first node, North Wind Avatar). Decision: choose the cards (one pick per card, may stop early unless mandatory); the found card is revealed where the card says so (no rules effect)."},
	{"op:ChooseCard", "OpChooseCard (Obj player, F, C code)", "Player Obj chooses a card matching F (zone in the filter), stored as RefChosen; a mandatory ask is posed with one candidate too and none with no candidate. C 1: up to one (a Done beside the cards); C 2: RememberChosen$; C 3: the Peek's top-A library window. C 4 / 5 (chooseAttachPick / chooseAttachPickOpt): the object-side Attach pick, always followed by an AttachObj with C = RefChosen: the candidates are the F permanents other than that AttachObj's destination (none when the destination is gone); none: no ask, nothing chosen; C 4 (mandatory) with one candidate: taken unasked; otherwise the ask, with a Done for C 5 (Optional$ is the pick's Min 0). Gorge: effAttach with Choices$ and no Object$ (the pool of battlefieldValidTargets, destCandidatesFor, one KChoose). Zack Fair, Vow to Erebor, Winter Soldier, Icy Assassin. C 6 (choosePutCounterPick): PutCounter's Choices$ recipient pick, always followed by an OpPutCounter on RefChosen: a CounterNum$ amount <= 0 or no F permanent: no ask, nothing chosen; one candidate: taken unasked; otherwise one mandatory ask (no Done) over the F permanents, seat 0's battlefield then seat 1's. Gorge: putCounterChooseTitled (Min 1, Max 1, ResumeKind counter_pick). Aerith Rescue Mission, Wick, the Whorled Mind. C 8 (chooseCopyPick): CopyPermanent's Choices$ pick, always followed by an ExtCopyPicked on RefChosen: one mandatory ask (no Done) over the F permanents, posed with one candidate too, none with no candidate; the ask is ChGenCopyPick, whose options gorge names \"permanent\" (copypermanent_choice). Calamity, Galloping Inferno. C 9 (choosePopulatePick): CopyPermanent Populate$ True (CR 701.36a), always followed by an ExtCopyPicked on RefChosen: F is the chooser's creature tokens; none: no ask, nothing chosen; one candidate: taken unasked; otherwise one mandatory ask (no Done) in the same ChGenCopyPick form as C 8. Gorge: effects/copypermanent.go's Populate$ arm. Rootborn Defenses, Trostani's Judgment. C 10 (chooseAttachDest): the destination-side Attach pick (effAttach with Object$ and Choices$), always followed by an AttachObj with Obj RefChosen and C RefRemembered: the candidates are the F permanents other than a lone remembered object still on the battlefield (none when no remembered object is); none: no ask, nothing chosen; one: taken unasked; otherwise one mandatory ask (no Done) over them in battlefield order. Gorge: effAttach's Choices$ pool with ObjectPresent (attachableBy, one KChoose, attachAll). Fumble."},
	{"op:PutCounter", "OpPutCounter (Obj permanent, A n, C counter kind, B remember mode)", "The battlefield permanent Obj gets `A` counters of kind C through the counter replacements, then CounterAddedOnce. B 1 (RememberAmount$): the landed count joins the resolution's remembered count. B 2 (RememberPut$): the recipient joins the remembered set when the CounterNum$ value is > 0, read before replacements (gorge does not ask that a counter landed). Gorge: effPutCounter (effects/counters_put.go, rememberPlaced). Systems Override."},
	{"op:ChooseMove", "OpChooseMove (Obj player, A count, C zone|SearchFlags<<3, F)", "Player chooses A cards matching F from their own graveyard or hand (F.Zone; F.Ctrl = owner), or permanents from either battlefield (a zoneless F: gorge effHiddenPick's game-wide public pool, seat 0 first, or with SrOwnZone player Obj's battlefield only; they leave for C&7), and moves them to zone `C&7`. Not targeted. Inspiration from Beyond (mandatory instant or sorcery to hand). From a hand (gorge effChangeZoneHand, ChGenHandMove): SrConfirm poses gorge's Optional$ yes/no confirmation first (ChGenConfirm; no skips the move); a SrMandatory move with no more eligible cards than A takes them all unasked; SrTapped enters them tapped, SrRemember remembers them (RememberChanged$); Obj may be a target player whose hand it is (effChangeZoneHandOwners), SrChooserYou then asks the controller (Chooser$ You). SrReveal with zone none is a reveal pick (gorge effReveal: ChGenReveal, option kind reveal; nothing moves, SrRemember remembers the pick; SrConfirm then asks only when a card qualifies). Arboreal Grazer, Aether Vial, Castigate, Armored Kincaller."},
	{"op:ChangeZoneAllEx", "OpChangeZoneAllEx (Obj player or none, C zone|MoveFlags<<3, F)", "Move every card matching F (F.Zone = origin) to zone `C&7`. Obj (a target player) restricts to that player's cards (Angel of Finality: exile target player's graveyard). MvUnderYourControl: onto the battlefield under the controller's control (Rise of the Dark Realms, from all graveyards). MvEntryRiders (onto the battlefield; A = constant counter count | counter kind<<8, B = override index+1, 0 = none): each entrant, as it enters and before any of the sweep's enters checks fire, gets A counters of that kind (WithCountersType$, CR 122.6) and a permanent override record (StaticEffect$ Affected$ Card.IsRemembered, CR 603.6b; gorge applyStaticEffect per moved card). Ghost Vacuum. MvForgetOther (non-battlefield, non-library origin, ForgetOtherRemembered$): the matched set is copied out in scan order, the remembered set is cleared (both halves), then the copy moves, MvRemember re-remembering each (Random Encounter). B bit kop.CzUntilLeaves (a battlefield to exile sweep, no entry riders; Duration$ UntilHostLeavesPlay, carried in B because every MoveFlags bit is taken): nothing moves once the source has left the battlefield, and each exiled non-token permanent is linked to the source (genState.links, full table: StallLinks) so it returns, in link order, when the source leaves (Pinnacle Starcage). With MvGraveExile and B = kop.CzLibrarySideboard the origin is every library then every sideboard (Library,Sideboard, Turtles Forever's put-back): the matching cards go on top of their owner's library in sweep order (library cards first). With MvGraveExile and B = kop.CzHandGrave the origin is every seat's hand, then every seat's graveyard (Hand,Graveyard: the cards sit in the library in that move order); with B&kop.CzShuffleEach the sweep ends with both libraries shuffled, the owner of the first card moved first, then the other seat (UseAllOriginZones$ with Shuffle$ True: Echo of Eons, Timetwister)."},
	{"op:DigEx", "OpDigEx (Obj player(s), A look, B take, C zone|DigFlags<<3, F)", "Player looks at the top A cards; chooses B of them matching F (B=-1: all of them, no choice; -2: any number) for zone `C&7`; the rest go to zone `(C>>3)&7` (Library = bottom unless DigRestTop; DigRestTopAsk: on top in the controller's order, one pick per card, the first on top). DigOptional: may take none. DigRandomOrder: the rest go to the bottom in a random order (uses the RNG; gorge's draw order). DigTakeToTop: the taken card goes on top (Gutless Plunderer, rest to graveyard). DigRemember: moved cards become RefRemembered. DigReveal/DigRevealToCtrl: reveal (no rules effect). Obj = RefEachPlayer runs for each player, the resolving controller first (gorge AliveFrom; Etali). Decision: the chosen subset (one pick per card)."},
	{"op:DigUntil", "OpDigUntil (Obj player(s), A count, C zone|DigUntilFlags<<3, F)", "Reveal cards from the top until A cards matching F are revealed (or the library runs out). Found cards go to zone `C&7`, the other revealed cards to `(C>>3)&7`; DuRestBottom: library bottom; DuRandomOrder: random order; DuFoundWithRevealed: no separate found destination — the found card goes with the rest (gorge effects/diguntil.go: absent FoundDestination$); DuFoundAttacking: a found card put onto the battlefield enters attacking (Attacking$ True). Consuming Aberration (each opponent, until a land, all to graveyard), Spinner of Souls (until a creature: to hand, rest bottom random; the trigger is optional)."},
	{"op:Peek", "OpPeek (Obj player, A)", "Player looks at the top A cards of their library (no reveal, a look_ack first); they become the remembered set. Curator of Destinies. C=PeekPublic: a public reveal with no ask (gorge effReveal), and with PeekRemember the cards join the remembered set (RememberRevealed$). Aven Windreader. C=PeekMayReveal: the top card of player Obj's library, when it matches F, is offered to that player (gorge effReveal reveal_optional yes/no, ChGenPeekReveal); a yes reveals it and appends it to the remembered set, a no or a non-matching or absent top card remembers nothing and asks nothing. Gathering Stone. C=PeekHand: every card in the hand of each player Obj names joins the remembered set in hand order, appended (RevealHand RememberRevealed$; an empty hand remembers nothing). Inquisition."},
	{"op:TwoPiles", "OpTwoPiles (C zone, B.N flags)", "Decisions: the separator splits the remembered cards into pile A and pile B (one pick per pile A card, Done-closed; a one-card set poses no split); the chooser picks a pile; the chosen pile goes to zone C (Hand) in its own order (pile A as picked, pile B as revealed), the other to the graveyard in the revealed order. The controller separates and the first live opponent picks under B.N&TpOppChooses (Separator$ You, Chooser$ Opponent); B.N&TpOppSeparates swaps them (Separator$ Opponent, the chooser Defined$ You, Fact or Fiction). With two or more live opponents the controller chooses WHICH opponent (CR 801.5b) and the answer is kept across the split; B.N&TpUnchosenPileOrder moves an unchosen pile A in pick order (a ChangeZone Defined$ Remembered body). More than 12 remembered cards stall StallLook. Curator of Destinies, Steam Augury, Fact or Fiction, Sphinx of Uthuun (gorge api:TwoPiles, DefinedCards$ Remembered)."},
	{"op:ChooseEachType", "OpChooseEachType (Obj players)", "Each player in Obj chooses, for each of artifact, battle, creature, enchantment, land, planeswalker, one permanent they control of that type if any (one object may satisfy several types); the chosen objects form RefChosen / F2ChosenCard. Liliana, Dreadhorde General -9 (followed by OpSacrificeAll of the opponents' nonchosen permanents)."},
	{"op:SacrificeAll", "OpSacrificeAll (F)", "Every permanent matching F is sacrificed by its controller, simultaneously. No decision."},
	{"op:CastFree", "OpCastFree (Obj cards, C zone|flags<<3, F)", "The controller may cast any number of the cards in Obj without paying their mana costs, during the resolution, in an order they choose; lands among them can't be played. Obj: RefRemembered (the remembered set), a target slot, or RefNone with F selecting cards in zone `C&7` (Exile / Hand / Graveyard, seat 0 then seat 1 in zone order). Flags: bit 3 AmountOne (close the ask after one pick), bit 4 ForgetPlayed (drop the begun card from the remembered set), bit 5 ReplaceGraveyard (exile the spell when it leaves the stack instead of the graveyard), bit 6 CopyCard (Play CopyCard$ True, CR 707.12: Obj is RefRemembered over cards in Exile; the original stays in exile and a copy is cast, an ofCopy object owned by the caster that gorge casts from its library holding zone (cast-from Library); a permanent card's copy resolves into a token (CR 707.10f), the copy ceases to exist leaving the stack (CR 704.5d); a multi-face card stalls StallCopyCast),, bit 7 Repeat (AllowRepeats$ True with Amount$ A, on a CopyCard cast: A is the copy count, evaluated at the pose; the remembered card stands A times in the offer and each pick queues one copy, so the ask can stop at any count; A below one offers nothing, more than eight copies stalls StallFree; gorge effects/play.go). Bit 8 Paid (a Play with no WithoutManaCost$, on a CopyCard cast of Obj RefSelf, the source card in exile: an exile-granted ability's 'create a copy of this card, you may cast the copy'): the copy pays its mana cost, through gorge's manual mana window with no payment plan (bflLowered); a copy whose mana cost the window cannot meet reverses there (CR 733.1), keeping the window's taps and ceasing the copy (CR 704.5d), bit 9 Amount (a literal Amount$ A: the ask closes after A picks), bit 10 SpellMV (a Play's ValidSA$ cmc bound read on the spell being cast, so a split card counts its front half, not the sum of its halves, CR 601.3a, 709.3a; a Valid$ cmc bound stays a card-in-zone read and keeps summing). Q, Stacking the Deck. Bloodthirsty Adversary, Reenact the Crime, Infinite Diversity. Each cast puts a spell on the stack above this ability. Decision loop: pick one of the remaining spell cards or stop (gorge offers one with no legal target too: its cast is refused and it stays exiled); targets/modes/X(=0) for each as cast. Etali, Primal Storm (P1); The Key to the Vault, Breaching Dragonstorm (P1); Daring Waverider (P2); Buster Sword, Lady Octopus (P3); Sword of Once and Future (P4)."},
	{"op:MayPlay", "OpMayPlay (Obj card, A duration, C zone|follows<<6)", "The controller may play Obj from zone C (cast it paying its costs, or play it as their land drop) until the duration ends: DurEOT this turn, DurYourNextTurn until the end of their next turn, DurWhileSrcMay for as long as the Effect's source stays on the battlefield (Duration$ AsLongAsControl; gorge reads the source's zone and controller, and a control change ends the grant for good: Lightning, Security Sergeant). By default the permission ends if the card leaves that zone: a version-tied record, which also models a ForgetOnMoved$ equal to C (Abbot of Keral Keep's exiled card), an ExileOnMoved$ (gorge effectMoveSweep ends the whole effect) and a zone-lifetime duration (WhileExiled, CR 611.2b: a \"for as long as\" duration does not restart). C bit 6 (MayPlayFollows, kgen lower_zone.go's continuous case): the record follows its card instead -- gorge's grant is a continuous effect over the remembered card (CR 611.2c), read every time the card is back in C within the duration and not consumed by its own cast, so Skyclave Shade cast from the graveyard and sacrificed back to it the same turn is offered again (its ForgetOnMoved$ Exile fires only on a move from exile, which kgen leaves to gorge). Chandra +2 / Strongbox Raider / Kellan (exiled card), Zul Ashur (target Zombie creature card in your graveyard), Skyclave Shade (follows). B bit 8 (MayPlayAdventure): the permission offers the Adventure face only (Mosswood Dreadknight)."},
	{"op:CreateEmblem", "OpCreateEmblem (Obj player, C emblem, A number)", "The player gets `Table.Emblems[C]` in the command zone: its abilities (a triggered ability with Trigger.Zone ZoneCommand, or a static) function from there for the rest of the game. An Effect's `StaticAbilities$ Mode$ CastWithFlash | ValidSA$ Spell | Caster$ You` body is a StatCastWithFlash static of the emblem (gorge effectFlashGrants): its player may cast the spells Filter names as though they had flash, until end of turn (Borne Upon a Wind, Alchemist's Refuge, Emergence Zone, Winding Canyons; Quicken) or until the controller's next turn (Teferi, Time Raveler's +1); an Effect's ForgetOnCast$ is the static's Filter2, and the first cast it names ends the whole emblem (Quicken's next sorcery; State.embFlashForget). A is the Effect's frozen chosen number (0 when unused): evaluated once against the resolving Effect's context and stored in `State.g.embN` (clamped to 0..255), the value an emblem static marked StEmbNum reads. Kaito -9 (whenever a player casts a spell, create a 2/1 Ninja), Vivien Reid -8 (creatures you control get +2/+2 and have vigilance, trample, indestructible). A no-RememberObjects$ `DB$ Effect` static of Mode$ ReduceCost (an EOT emblem: Goblin Maskmaker's face-down discount, which gorge never applies because it prices the face-down cast against the card in hand) or Mode$ CanAttackDefender with ValidCard$ Card.EffectSource (a WhileHost emblem, also from a triggered Effect with no Duration$: Territorial Witchstalker, Stalked Researcher, Krotiq Nestguard; CR 611.2a). When every static of the Effect is a ReduceCost whose Amount$ is the SVar Count$ChosenNumber, kgen reads SetChosenNumber$ through lc.value into A and marks those statics StEmbNum (no Static.VA): gorge evaluates the number once at resolution (effects/effect.go's state.ContinuousEffect.ChosenNumber) and the cost path reads the frozen field, so a life total that changes later in the turn does not raise the discount (Rowan, Scion of War; Will, Scion of Peace). Any other SetChosenNumber$ shape refuses. A is the frozen number only in the default case: an Emblem with CapturePlayer (an Effect's RememberObjects$ TargetedPlayer over a DamageDone trigger with ValidTarget$ Player.IsRemembered, Great Train Heist's third mode) stores the targeted player's seat + 1 in `State.g.embN`, and the DamageDone hook fires only when the damaged player is that seat.  An EOT Effect with ValidTgts$ Creature and RememberObjects$ Targeted over a DamageDone trigger whose ValidSource$ is Creature.IsRemembered sets Emblem.Capture to the chain's target slot: OpCreateEmblem stores that object + 1 in `State.g.embN` (no frozen number shares the emblem), the trigger's filter carries no Remembered flag, and the DamageDone hook fires only when the damage source is the stored object, queued with the damage dealt as TriggerAmount (gorge: Creature.IsRemembered over the delayed trigger's Remembered, TriggerCount$DamageAmount). The Inner Light's chapter II draws that many cards. An Effect that remembers its targeted creature and carries one static beside one trigger lowers in two shapes. A CantBlockBy static (ExileOnMoved$ Battlefield) beside a combat DamageDealtOnce trigger of the remembered creature is the unblockable record plus an emblem with Capture and CaptureLapse: the hook fires once per combat damage batch (the DamageDealtOnce latch) and the body's first Remembered read is the damage source (Long River Lurker's flicker). A CanAttackDefender static (ForgetOnMoved$ Battlefield) beside a DamageDone trigger whose ValidSource$ is Card.Self is a Capture emblem of that static alone, because gorge registers nothing for the Effect's own copy of the trigger (the Effect never deals damage): the static gate reads State.g.embN, so the grant reaches only the captured creature (The Pride of Hull Clade). CaptureLapse zeroes embN when the captured object leaves the battlefield (a returned object is new, CR 400.7). An EOT Effect with no RememberObjects$ whose DamageDone trigger has ValidSource$ Card.EffectSource sets Emblem.Capture to the Effect's own source object (Lyra, Tolarian Archangel's \"whenever Lyra deals combat damage to a player\"): the filter is the remembered spelling, gorge's EffectSource being the source object by id, which a source that left and returned keeps. An EOT Effect with no RememberObjects$ whose DamageDone trigger has ValidSource$ Card.ChosenCardStrict, after the chain's one ChooseCard, sets Emblem.Capture to RefChosen (Azra Oddsmaker's \"whenever that creature deals combat damage to a player this turn\"): OpCreateEmblem stores the chosen creature when the emblem is made, before the chain's ClearChosenCard$ empties the set, as gorge registers the trigger over the chosen cards at the Effect. An Effect that remembers more than the one Targeted creature lowers in three more shapes (kop.Emblem; dirac/static_emblemrem.go, trig_emblemonce.go, trig_emblemrem.go). A permanent Effect with RememberObjects$ Remembered over a one-off Phase$ Upkeep trigger, in a spell or ability whose chain wrote the remembered set (The Eagles Are Coming!): A is the set's size (RememberedCount, frozen in State.g.embN), NumAmount carries it as each trigger's amount (the body's Remembered$Amount lowers to TriggerAmount, and any other Remembered read in the body refuses) and Once drops the emblem after the trigger first fires, as gorge's one-shot delayed trigger. An end-of-turn Effect with RememberObjects$ Targeted over a ChangesZone Battlefield-to-Graveyard trigger of ValidCard$ Creature.IsRemembered, over a chain of exactly two single battlefield target slots and no ValidTgts$ of its own (T'Pring, Never Parted): Capture and Capture2 are the two slots' objects (g.embN and g.embR, object + 1), the trigger's filter carries no Remembered flag and the dies hook fires only for a remembered object, queued as the creating card's latent copy; the Effect's ConditionDefined$ Targeted | ConditionPresent$ Creature | ConditionCompare$ EQ2 gate lowers to a SkipIf over both slots (RefMatches each, a moved card read as a card in its new zone). A permanent Effect with RememberObjects$ RememberedLKI, ForgetOnMoved$ Battlefield and a Card.EffectSource leave trigger over the tokens its resolution made (Mysterio, Master of Illusion): CaptureRem stores the resolution's remembered set (up to four objects in the emblem's slots, g.embN, g.embR and g.embX; a fifth stalls StallEmbRem), CaptureLapse drops an object when it leaves the battlefield, Source fires the leave trigger for the object that made the emblem alone, and the body (exactly the exile of Remembered from the battlefield) becomes OpExt ExtExileEmbRem over the objects the trigger carries. NotHere makes the emblem only while its host is off the battlefield: gorge ends a permanent Effect registered by a battlefield permanent with that incarnation (delayedRegistrationLive, SourceBattlefield), so Mysterio's leave trigger never fires when it was on the battlefield as the Effect was made, and fires, exiling the tokens it remembered, only for a registration made while it was gone (it died with its enters trigger on the stack) when that object leaves again. An EOT Effect over a Mode$ DamageDoneOnce line with ValidTarget$ Player (Aphelia, Viper Whisperer) is the per-referent batch DamageDone emblem line (Tf2Batch + Tf2PerReferent): gorge's delayed-trigger path latches the damage batch per damaged player, and the emblem hook does too through the step's refLatch, so two sources hitting one player in a step fire the body once; a DamageAmount$ gate refuses."},
	{"op:Override", "OpOverride (Obj, A duration, C override)", "Apply `Table.Overrides[C]` to Obj for DurEOT, DurPermanent (until it leaves the battlefield) or DurUntilYourNextTurn (until the resolving controller's next turn begins: it ends at the cleanup before that turn, gorge UntilYourNextTurn; Azure Beastbinder). Override records apply in a fixed order: set types/subtypes/colours and lose-abilities, then add types/subtypes/keywords, set P/T before counters and pumps (CR 613 layers 4/5/6/7b collapsed into a fixed order — the plan's replacement for a layer system). Grant[i] (ability index+1 of the APPLYING card) is an ability the object gains. Landwalk (a land FilterID) is a Pump KW$ Landwalk:<spec> granted until end of turn: the object can't be blocked while the defending player controls a land matching it (gorge combat.LandwalkEvades over the derived keywords; a layer-6 grant, so a later loss of all abilities ends it). Piracy Charm. Users: Fake Your Own Death (grant a dies trigger, EOT), Kellan (becomes Human Faerie Detective / 3/2 Rogue with double strike, permanent, after a SkipUnless on its current subtype), Mild-Mannered Librarian (becomes a Werewolf), Soulstone Sanctuary (a 3/3 creature land with vigilance and all creature types), Infernal Vessel / Valkyrie's Call (the returned card is also a Demon / an Angel with flying)."},
	{"op:ReflexiveTrigger", "OpReflexiveTrigger (A count, C ability)", "'When you do': put this card's latent ability C on the stack A times (A=0: not at all); its targets are chosen as it is put on the stack, after the current resolution step. Faebloom Trick: A = tokens created / 2 (ExTokensCreated, Div 2), then tap target creature an opponent controls. B: the value the body reads as TriggerRemembered$ (Amount / CardManaCost / GreatestCardManaCost of the remembered set), evaluated in the parent's context as the trigger is put on the stack and carried as the entry's trigger amount; the zero Const (every other reflexive trigger) carries 0. Ill-Timed Explosion (X damage to each creature, X the highest mana value among the discarded cards: its Discard<> unless-cost, B=kop.PayBRemember, remembers what it discards), The Ancient One (mill equal to the discarded card's mana value), Miasma Demon (up to that many targets). Obj (RememberObjects$ Targeted): a target ref of the parent; the target's object and ver, when it is still the chosen object on the battlefield, ride the entry as trigObj and trigAmt (B is then the zero Const), and the body's Fight Defined$ DelayTriggerRemembered fights nothing once that object's ver has moved (a zone change makes a new object, CR 400.7; gorge effImmediateTrigger), where a body Bite from it (DealDamage DamageSource$ DelayTriggerRemembered NumDmg$ TriggerRemembered$CardPower) deals the creature's last known power, snapshotted into the entry's LKI record as it is put on the stack (CR 608.2h; gorge rules rememberedPTLKI). Novel Nunchaku, Curse of the Werefox, Thorin, Mountain-king."},
	{"op:DelayedProgram", "OpDelayedProgram (Obj objects, A timing, C ability)", "Register a delayed trigger: at the beginning of the next end step (anyone's; A = 0), the next upkeep of any player (A = kop.DelayUpkeep: gorge Phase$ Upkeep, ValidPlayer$ Player, the slowtrips' NextTurn$ True) the controller's next upkeep (A = kop.DelayYourUpkeep: ValidPlayer$ You) or the next end of combat step (A = kop.DelayEndCombat: Phase$ EndCombat), after that step's Phase triggers, or the remembered object's next battlefield-to-graveyard move this turn (A = kop.DelayDiesThisTurn: gorge Mode$ ChangesZone, ValidCard$ Card.IsTriggerRemembered, ThisTurn$ True; after the move's dies/leaves triggers; one-shot, dropped at the turn change), run this card's latent ability C with RefDelayedRemembered = the objects in Obj as they are now (cards that later change zones are still found). Kykar's blink (return the exiled card), Nine-Lives Familiar (return with one fewer revival counter). B = DpTrack registers the program tracked to the resolving source's object (Decayed's end-of-combat sacrifice): it is ordered with the other due triggers and, if that object has left, resolves doing nothing. B = DpMany registers the resolution's whole remembered set (up to four objects) for a body of OpBounce with BncDelayedMany, which returns each still on the battlefield to hand (Random Encounter: ChangeZoneAll ForgetOtherRemembered$ then a RememberObjects$ Remembered delayed trigger). The same program carries a RememberedLKI target slot of several objects (Hide on the Ceiling, Temporal Tribulation, Eerie Interlude: one Exile of the slot with RememberChanged$) for a body of OpReturn with kop.RetDelayedMany (Origin$ Exile), which returns every object still the one registered to the battlefield in registration order as one entering event."},
	{"op:GiveGift", "OpGiveGift", "The controller gives a gift (CR 702.174b): fire \"whenever you give a gift\" triggers (TrigGiveGift, Jolly Gerbils). The gift itself follows as ordinary ops (the GiftAbility body: a card for the opponent, a Food, a tapped Fish), the block guarded by CondPromised at the head of an instant's or sorcery's program (gorge rules/stack.go splices the GiftAbility at the head of the spell's chain and emits events.GiveGift just before it)."},
	{"op:BecomeCopy", "OpBecomeCopy (Obj replaced, F choices, A grant override, B.N BecomeCopyCtr, C optional|override<<1)", "As-enters replacement program (an ETBReplacement keyword line): while the permanent spell is on the stack about to resolve, its controller is asked the clone choice (DkChoose ChGenClone): each battlefield permanent matching F (seat 0's battlefield, then seat 1's, in entry order; F's mana-value bound may read ExCastManaSpent), then, when C&1 (the keyword line's :Optional) or nothing matches, \"enter as itself\" (mode 1, source = the spell). A pick makes the permanent enter as a copy of it (CR 707.2, 614.1c): the copied card's copiable values (its own copy, if it is one, and its copy exceptions) with B's exceptions as copiable values (CpFlying: flying; the subtype added, CR 707.9b); its triggered abilities see it enter. Entered any other way (not cast) nothing is asked and it enters as itself. Gorge: rules/cast_etbchoice.go collectETBChoices kind copy, effects/clone.go effClone (CloneEnter.ETB). The copied card's enters-tapped property, its printed K:etbCounter counters (CR 707.5) and its enters programs apply (a choice among them is asked once it has entered, not with the clone choice). Templates are creatures and artifacts only (kgen refuses an Aura or planeswalker template). The exceptions (C>>1, an override index+1) are read through copyExceptions like CopyPermanent's: AddTypes$ lists (card types, supertypes, subtypes), AddKeywords$, SetPower$/SetToughness$, AddColors$, SetColor$, NonLegendary$ (Visage Bandit, Glasspool Mimic, Phyrexian Metamorph, Quicksilver Gargantuan); NewName$ and AddKeywords$ Changeling (a CDA, gorge clone.go L531) refuse. B.N bit BecomeCopyCtr (kop.BecomeCopyCtr): the remembered copy origin's counters ride into the entering copy as it enters (Dominion Saboteur: RememberCloneOrigin$ True then PutCounter CounterType$ EachFromSource EachFromSource$ Remembered; CR 707.9b, 614.12), folded from the whole rider chain by kgen, on top of the template's own printed counters. B.N bit BecomeCopyEmbalm (kop.BecomeCopyEmbalm): Embalm$ True (Vizier of Many Faces: \"except if CARDNAME was embalmed, the token has no mana cost, it's white, and it's a Zombie\"; CR 707.9b), the C>>1 exceptions (only AddTypes$, SetColor$, RemoveCost$ ride it; kgen refuses any other beside it, a RemoveCost$ outside an Embalm$ True body, and an Embalm$ other than True, gorge clone_params.go) apply only when the entering object is a token whose copiable values already carry the no-mana-cost copy exception (the embalm mint's, read before the template's exceptions join; gorge effects/clone.go cloneEmbalmGate, cloneEmbalmProvenance): the kernel puts that mint's exceptions on the token's slot ahead of its as-enters copy (copyTokenEnterFrom, embalmMint); a hard-cast carrier or any other token copy of the card is a plain copy. A (an override index+1, 0: none): AddAbilities$ (Mercurial Pretender), the named SVars lowered as latent activated abilities of the entering card, applied to the copy as a permanent override record sourced from the printed card once a template is picked (gorge clone.go folds the grant into the copy's copiable values, CR 707.9b, so a copy of the copy has it too, CR 707.3; the kernel carries the record to a later copy of the copy, copyGrantsAdd, drops it when a newer copy layer covers the copy and re-derives it on a re-base, and reads the ability from the card that made the record, grantCardAt)."},
	{"op:GainControl", "OpGainControl (Obj, A.N duration, B.N GcUntap|GcHasteEOT, C new-controller Ref)", "The new controller (C: RefNone = the resolving controller, RefOpponent/RefEachOpponent, a player target slot, or the trigger's player / the trigger object's controller: NewController$ TriggeredTarget, TriggeredActivator, TriggeredSourceController; Clambassadors, Drooling Ogre, Contested War Zone) gains control of Obj (CR 613.1b layer 2); Obj RefNone with a filter F is AllValid$: every battlefield permanent F admits, listed in object order before any control moves, each gets the same record (Varchild, Betrayer of Kjeldor; Tevesh Szat, Doom of Fools). A.N: DurEOT (CR 514.2), DurPermanent, DurYourNextTurn (to the end of the effect controller's next turn), DurWhileSource (LoseControl$ LeavesPlay: while the source stays on the battlefield), DurWhileControlSource (LeavesPlay,LoseControl: and while the effect's controller controls it); a source-bound duration already over at resolution does nothing (CR 611.2b). Each effect is a timestamped control record: when records end the object goes to the newest surviving record's controller, or to the controller before the earliest record (gorge expireControl); a source-bound record is checked by the state-based check. Riders: GcUntap untaps it (a stun counter is removed instead), GcHasteEOT gives haste until end of turn. GcHasteEOT on any longer duration gives haste for as long as the control record lives (AddKWs$ Haste beside any other LoseControl$: Slave of Bolas; Evil's Thrall's second node). Sower of Temptation, Act of Treason variants, Donate. With Obj RefRemembered over several remembered objects each one still on the battlefield is taken, in remembered order (gorge effGainControl walks its Defined set): Fumble's Auras and Equipment."},
	{"op:ClassLevelUp", "OpClassLevelUp (Obj self, A level)", "The resolving ability's source Class becomes level `A` (CR 716.2a): its CtrLevel count (level-1, a kind above NumCounterKinds2 that no counter census, doubling or projection sees) is set to `A-1`, and \"when this Class becomes level N\" triggers fire (TrigCounterAddedOnce with N = CtrLevel, gated Eq on the new level). Nothing when the source has left the battlefield or is already at level `A` or more. No decision. Gorge: effects/class_level.go effClassLevelUp (a designation, not a counter)."},
	{"op:ClearRemembered", "OpClearRemembered", "Forget the resolution's remembered set (RefRemembered)."},
	{"op:ClearChosen", "OpClearChosen", "Forget the chosen card(s) (RefChosen)."},
	{"op:DoubleCounters", "OpDoubleCounters (Obj, C kind)", "Put on each object in Obj as many counters of kind C as it has (C=255: do that for every kind it has). Mossborn Hydra (+1/+1 on itself), Zimone (every kind, up to two targets)."},
	{"op:RemoveCounterRem", "OpRemoveCounterRem (Obj, A, C kind)", "Remove up to A counters of kind C from Obj; the number actually removed becomes ExRememberedCount (Fishing Pole: 'remove a bait counter. If you do, create a Fish')."},
	{"ext:EnterAttacking", "OpExt ExtEnterAttacking (Obj RefReplaced)", "Replacement program, after OpEnterTapped: the entering object enters attacking the controller's opponent (CR 508.4, 614.12; never declared, so no Attacks trigger), only in the controller's own declare attackers..end of combat. Kira Nerys, Firebrand's `R:Event$ Moved` with `IsPresent$ Creature.attacking+YouCtrl` and a `DB$ ChangeZone | Defined$ ReplacedCard | Tapped$ True | Attacking$ True` body; two or more CR 508.4 defenders stall (StallTokAtkAsk)."},
	{"op:EnterTapped", "OpEnterTapped (Obj RefReplaced)", "Replacement program: the entering object enters tapped (CR 614.1c). Used by ReplOthersEnterProgram (Authority of the Consuls); a self enters-tapped is ReplEntersTapped."},
	{"op:EnterWithCounters", "OpEnterWithCounters (Obj RefReplaced, A, C kind)", "Replacement program: the entering object enters with A counters of kind C (CR 614.1c, CR 122.6: the object enters with them). Whether CounterAddedOnce triggers (Wildwood Scourge, Exemplar of Light) see these counters: mirror gorge, the oracle decides. Conditional/X forms: Gnarlid Colony (kicked), Goblin Boarders (raid), Nine-Lives Familiar (cast by you), Wildwood Scourge (X), Banner of Kinship (count of the chosen type), Giada (other Angels, count of Angels you control)."},
	{"op:CopyAsTokenEx", "OpCopyAsTokenEx (Obj, A count, B.N CopyFlags, C exception override+1)", "The controller creates A tokens that are copies of Obj (copiable values: its card's printed characteristics, CR 707.2; a copy of a card in exile/graveyard copies the card). C names the copy exceptions (CR 707.9b) as a Table.Overrides record: set P/T (Offspring's 1/1, SetPower$/SetToughness$), added keywords (AddKeywords$: Chandra's haste; AddKeywords$ Changeling: every creature type, Dominion Infiltration), an added subtype (AddTypes$: Abyssal Harvester's Nightmare), added card types and supertypes (AddTypes$: Artifact, Creature & Balloon, Legendary; the types are ORed into the base types at layer 1), added colours (AddColors$, after any set colour), AddStaticAbilities$ naming one equip cost reduction of the copy itself (GrantStatics: an OvGate bit that switches on the reduction lowerPool adds to every pool card with an Equip ability; Firion, Wild Rose Warrior), and NonLegendary$ (the copy's type line loses Legendary, applied after the added types; the legend rule reads the derived types, so the copy and its legendary original coexist; gorge copypermanent.go removeLegendary). They are the copy's layer-1 copiable values, so a copy of the copy inherits them and a later set-P/T effect overrides the 1/1 only while it lasts. CpSacAtEnd: at the beginning of the next end step, sacrifice it (Chandra +1, Electroduplicate). CpSacAtUpkeep (both CpSacAtEndDly and CpExileAtEnd; AtEOT$ SacrificeUpkeep): the untracked one-shot sacrifice at the beginning of the next upkeep of any player (delayed.when dlyUpkeep; Firion). B.N >> CopyPumpShift: PumpKeywords$, an override record (index+1) of a permanent keyword grant on each token after it enters; it is NOT a copy exception, so a copy of the token lacks it; with CopyPumpEOT (PumpDuration$ EOT: Gray and Adira, God-Pharaoh's Gift) the grant lasts until end of turn. CpRemember: the tokens become RefRemembered. CpExileAtEnd: at the beginning of the next end step, exile it (AtEOT$ Exile: Stormsplitter, Splinter Twin; gorge scheduleAtEOT). CpExileAtCombat (both CpSacAtEnd and CpExileAtEnd; AtEOT$ ExileCombat): the tracked exile at this turn's end of combat (Flamerush Rider). CpTapped: the token enters tapped (TokenTapped$ True: Replicator). CopyNonRemCtrl (bit 15): the tokens are created for each living player but the copied permanent's last-known controller, owner by owner from the controller (Controller$ NonRememberedController over a RememberLKI$ capture, or NonTargetedController over Defined$ Targeted's target snapshot: Fractured Identity's old and new scripts). Users also Self-Reflection, Homunculus Horde, Extravagant Replication."},
	{"op:CreateTokenEx", "OpCreateTokenEx (Obj, A, B.N TokenFlags|(Ref<<8), C token)", "OpCreateToken with TokRemember: the number created is readable as ExTokensCreated (Faebloom Trick). TokTapped as TrTapped. TokAttach: the token enters attached to the object B.N's high byte names (RefTarget0..2 or RefSelf, kop.TokAttachDest); it is not created when that object is not on the battlefield (CR 303.4g, gorge auraTokenWithheld) or when nothing on the board can be enchanted (gorge auraTokenGate), and the attach is not checked for legality (the CR 704.5m SBA removes an illegal attachment). A Role token's attach first sweeps every other Role off the bearer (CR 303.7a, gorge's attach-time sweep; static_roletokens.go). Both TokSacAtEnd and TokExileAtEnd set: an extended AtEOT$ rider, its kind in B.N's high byte (kop.TokAtEOTDestroy: destroy the token at the beginning of the next end step, tracked, indestructible and regeneration apply; kop.TokAtEOTSacCombat: sacrifice it at this turn's end of combat, untracked; kop.TokAtEOTExileCombat: exile it at this turn's end of combat, tracked; kop.TokAtEOTSacYourUpkeep: sacrifice it, untracked, at the beginning of its controller's next upkeep; gorge effects/ateot.go; trig_tokenateot.go); never with TokAttach. TokRememberSrc (B.N bit 15, as a uint16 image): each token remembers the creating source object (RememberSource$ True) as a per-source smRem record keyed by the token, which an ExSrcRemCounters expression reads (Saproling Burst: dirac/zone_tokrem.go); it shares the high byte with a destination Ref or AtEOT kind, so a script that needs either beside it stays refused."},
}
